# TypeScript / React / 3D

- TypeScript strict; no unreviewed `any`, unsafe casts, or silent error swallowing. Keep rendering/React components separate from transport acquisition and neuroscience.
- Validate untrusted network messages at runtime against shared contracts; TS interfaces alone are not runtime validation.
- Model units, time semantics and confidence/quality explicitly; do not show source estimates as direct cortical readings or uncalibrated probabilities as facts.
- Decouple GPU frame rate from EEG acquisition frequency; throttle visual updates without dropping raw recordings.
- Prefer accessible interactions; include loading, missing stream, degraded quality and reconnection states; dispose GPU resources and event listeners.
- Add Vitest tests for nontrivial logic and component behavior; use integration/e2e tests for protocol and streaming paths.
